# Documentation maintenance

Whenever you **implement or materially change** behavior (features, routes, validation, edge functions, DB schema/migrations, env vars, integrations, or user-visible flows), **update documentation in the same change**, not as a follow-up the user must request.

**Claude Code / skill picker:** invoke **`documentation-maintenance`** (and **`route-guides`** for page/section changes) before claiming done — Claude cannot auto-load this always-on `.mdc`. SessionStart + PostToolUse hooks also remind after code edits under `ui/` / `supabase/functions/` / `supabase/migrations/`.

## What to update

| Change type                                                                                                                       | Update                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |
| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Architecture, routes, env vars, API surface, data model, flows, deployment                                                        | **`docs/architecture/overview.md`** (full-app picture) and **`docs/PROJECT.md`** (topic index / API / env). Adjust the relevant section(s); add new tables/rows if you add endpoints or columns                                                                           |
| Shipped / cancelled backlog items, new roadmap tasks                                                                              | **GitHub Issues** + [`docs/README.md`](../docs/README.md) (Product backlog section); shipped history in `docs/archive/todos/shipped/`                                                                                                                                     |
| Anything about the **new booking flow redesign** (status machine, admin dashboard, Gmail listener, SD refund cron, new emails)    | **`docs/archive/planning/NEW_FLOW_PLAN.md`** — update the plan as decisions land, answered questions, and phases ship. Also flip items to answered / in progress / done                                                                                                   |
| Database migration or one-shot backfill instructions                                                                              | **`docs/archive/operations/migration-runbook.md`** (create when Phase 0 lands)                                                                                                                                                                                            |
| Global conventions agents rely on (paths, stack, “where things live”)                                                             | **`.cursor/rules/project-context.mdc`** if the old text would mislead future sessions                                                                                                                                                                                     |
| New Edge Function patterns or JWT/CORS policy                                                                                     | **`.cursor/rules/supabase-edge-functions.mdc`** if the shared contract changed                                                                                                                                                                                            |
| Booking status / transition / side-effect matrix changes                                                                          | **`.cursor/rules/booking-workflow.mdc`** — this file is canonical                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
| Admin auth rules, allow list, or new admin endpoints                                                                              | **`.cursor/rules/admin-auth.mdc`**                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |
| Page/section behavior, save flows, validation, per-route UX                                                                       | **`docs/guides/routes/*.md`** — see **`.cursor/rules/route-guides.mdc`** and **`.cursor/skills/route-guides/SKILL.md`**                                                                                                                                                   |
| **Pricing plans / tier catalog / `planPresentation` / entitlements**                                                              | **`/for-hosts/pricing`** (live via `list-public-pricing-plans` + shared `planPresentation.ts`) **and** **`docs/architecture/plans-feature-matrix.md`** + host Plans route guides (`org/plans.md` — the only in-app Plans page, billing is org-level only; `for-hosts.md`) |
| **New host feature (Plans and/or Team RBAC)**                                                                                     | **`plans-and-permissions`** skill + always-on **`.cursor/rules/plans-and-permissions.mdc`** — decide both or mark N/A in the same change                                                                                                                                  |
| **New / changed mutating capability** (edge write, workflow transition, cron, webhook, direct-write surface, guest/public action) | **`audit-logging`** skill + always-on **`.cursor/rules/audit-logging.mdc`** — emit an `activity_log` event via `_shared/activityLog.ts`, or mark `activity-log: N/A — <why>`, in the same change                                                                          |
| **UI layout, modals, menus, navigation, or mobile chrome** in `ui/src/**`                                                         | Invoke **`mobile-responsive`** skill + follow **`.cursor/rules/mobile-native-ui.mdc`** (always-on gate) and **`mobile-responsive.mdc`**; route guide if page UX changed                                                                                                   |

## Rules of thumb

- Prefer **small, accurate edits** over rewriting the whole doc unless the feature is cross-cutting.
- If you add a **new query param, env var, or HTTP route**, document it in `docs/PROJECT.md` (API tables or env sections).
- If behavior **diverges** from what `docs/PROJECT.md` says, **fix the doc**—do not leave contradictions.
- Per-route guides belong in **`docs/guides/routes/`** (mirrors app URLs). Use **`docs/guides/_template.md`** for new pages; update **`docs/guides/routes/README.md`** when adding routes.
- Operations runbooks live in **`docs/archive/operations/`**; active plans in **`docs/workflow/planned/`**; legacy in **`docs/archive/`**. Index: **`docs/README.md`**.
- Do **not** create extra markdown outside `docs/` (and subfolders), `scripts/README.md`, and `.cursor/rules/` unless the user asked for them.

## When docs need no change

Trivial fixes (typos, formatting, rename of internal variable with no API/UX impact) do not require doc updates unless they touch documented names.
